# Frontend Frameworks

## Tổng quan So sánh

| Aspect | Next.js | Nuxt.js | Vue.js |
|--------|---------|---------|--------|
| Framework | React | Vue | Vue (Core) |
| SSR | Yes (built-in) | Yes (built-in) | SPA / SSR (via Nuxt) |
| Routing | File-based (App Router) | File-based | Vue Router |
| Data Fetching | Server Components, fetch | useFetch, useAsyncData | Composables |
| State | React Query, Context, Zustand | Pinia, useState | Pinia, Composition API |
| Ecosystem | Vercel, large community | Nuxt modules | Vue ecosystem |

---

## 1. Next.js (React Framework)

### Mục tiêu

Next.js là React framework được sử dụng rộng rãi cho việc xây dựng các web applications hiện đại với features như Server-Side Rendering (SSR), Static Site Generation (SSG), và API routes. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, Next.js đóng vai trò là primary frontend framework cho các dự án cần SEO tốt, performance cao, và developer experience tuyệt vời.

### Nguyên tắc

**1. Rendering Strategy Selection**

SSG cho static content (homepage, blog posts). SSR cho dynamic, personalized content. ISR cho content that changes but can be cached. CSR cho highly interactive, user-specific content.

**2. App Router vs Pages Router**

Use App Router for new projects. It's the future of Next.js. Better data fetching with Server Components. Built-in layouts and nested routing.

**3. Server Components by Default**

Start with Server Components. Move to Client Components only when needed: Interactive UI (useState, useEffect), Browser APIs, Real-time data.

**4. Data Fetching Patterns**

Use async/await in Server Components. Fetch data close to where it's used. Use React `cache()` for request deduplication.

**5. Route Organization**

Group related routes together. Use route groups for layout organization. Use dynamic routes for parameterized URLs.

**6. API Routes for BFF**

Use API routes as Backend-For-Frontend. Aggregate data from multiple sources. Keep API routes thin.

### Checklist

- [ ] Next.js version selected (latest stable)
- [ ] Rendering strategy defined per page
- [ ] App Router structure established
- [ ] Data fetching patterns implemented
- [ ] Image optimization configured
- [ ] Metadata management setup
- [ ] Error handling implemented
- [ ] Loading states designed
- [ ] Testing strategy defined
- [ ] Deployment configuration ready

### Anti Pattern

**1. Overusing Client Components** - Marking everything as 'use client' increases bundle size unnecessarily.

**2. Data Fetching in Client Components** - Fetching data on client when server fetch is possible.

**3. Ignoring Loading States** - Not implementing proper loading UI causes layout shifts.

**4. Large Bundle Sizes** - Importing entire libraries without tree shaking.

### Best Practice

```typescript
// app/
// ├── (marketing)/
// │   ├── layout.tsx
// │   ├── page.tsx
// │   ├── about/
// │   └── pricing/
// ├── (dashboard)/
// │   ├── layout.tsx
// │   ├── dashboard/
// │   └── settings/
// ├── api/
// │   ├── users/
// │   └── orders/
// ├── layout.tsx
// └── not-found.tsx
```

```typescript
// Server Component Data Fetching
export default async function OrdersPage() {
  const [orders, user] = await Promise.all([
    getOrders(),
    getUser()
  ]);
  
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Orders for {user.name}</h1>
      <Suspense fallback={<OrderListSkeleton />}>
        <OrderList orders={orders} />
      </Suspense>
    </div>
  );
}
```

