## 4. Frontend Architecture

### Mục tiêu

Frontend Architecture là cách tổ chức và design frontend applications để đảm bảo scalability, maintainability, và performance. Focus trên component design, state management, routing, và user experience.

### Nguyên tắc

**1. Component Architecture** - Atomic design principles. Reusable components. Composable patterns.

**2. State Management** - Single source of truth. Predictable state updates. Separation of concerns.

**3. Routing** - Client-side routing. Lazy loading. Nested routes. Route guards.

**4. Data Fetching** - Server state vs client state. Caching strategies. Optimistic updates.

**5. Performance** - Code splitting. Lazy loading. Memoization. Virtual scrolling.

**6. Accessibility** - Semantic HTML. ARIA attributes. Keyboard navigation.

**7. Error Handling** - Error boundaries. Graceful degradation. User feedback.

### Checklist

- [ ] Project structure defined
- [ ] Component library established
- [ ] State management configured
- [ ] Routing implemented
- [ ] Data fetching strategy defined
- [ ] Error handling implemented
- [ ] Testing strategy defined
- [ ] Accessibility reviewed
- [ ] Performance optimized
- [ ] Documentation created

### Best Practice

```typescript
// Feature-based structure
// features/
// ├── auth/
// │   ├── components/
// │   ├── hooks/
// │   ├── services/
// │   └── types/
// ├── orders/
// │   ├── components/
// │   ├── hooks/
// │   └── types/
// └── products/
```

```typescript
// State Management with React Query
export const queryClient = new QueryClient({
  defaultOptions: {
    queries: {
      staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,
      gcTime: 10 * 60 * 1000,
      retry: 3,
    }
  }
});

// Zustand Store
export const useCartStore = create<CartState>()(
  persist(
    (set, get) => ({
      items: [],
      addItem: (item) => { /* ... */ },
      removeItem: (id) => { /* ... */ },
    }),
    { name: 'cart-storage' }
  )
);
```

